# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# requirements.in  --  the ONLY file you edit by hand.
#
# You never `pip install` from this file directly. You compile it into
# requirements.txt with `make lock`, which produces exact versions + SHA256
# hashes for EVERY package, including transitive dependencies.
#
# Why: this is "dependency pinning". It is the single cheapest defence against
# supply-chain attacks (a maintainer account gets hijacked, a new version of a
# tiny transitive dep starts stealing your API keys, etc.).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

